{"skill":{"slug":"google-workspace-mcp","displayName":"Google Workspace (No Cloud Console)"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1769458839920,"changelog":"Initial release of Google Workspace skill with zero setup complexity:\n\n- Access Gmail, Calendar, Drive, Docs, Sheets, Slides, Chat, and more — no Google Cloud Console required, just OAuth sign-in.\n- Install and configure instantly with a single command; credentials managed automatically.\n- Includes 49 tools for searching, reading, creating, updating, and sending within all major Google Workspace apps.\n- Simple troubleshooting and re-authentication workflows provided.\n- Example commands for common actions included in documentation.","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":4657,"sha256":"bfe848d8a0f1375bf6c9f6f4eb94eced1566b3724231a78c15e1718194bb5ec0","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2046,"sha256":"480f782e055c1d7989d6e7a0d14c4a69b0e97517a9bcb985e55e17fbe80403e3","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789021582031,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"b8c80751965069ae86f77f0533d207ae26a4e8fb0266ae8094bc37778b0946aa","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/b8c80751965069ae86f77f0533d207ae26a4e8fb0266ae8094bc37778b0946aa","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: google-workspace-mcp\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill is classified as suspicious due to its broad access to Google Workspace data and its reliance on executing an external npm package (`@presto-ai/google-workspace-mcp`) via `npm install -g` and `npx`, which introduces a supply chain risk. While the capabilities like downloading files (`drive.downloadFile`, `gmail.downloadAttachment`) and sending emails/messages are plausibly needed for a comprehensive Google Workspace integration, they represent significant risky capabilities. No explicit prompt injection attempts against the AI agent or other clear malicious intent are found in the `SKILL.md` or `_meta.json` files themselves.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779160060446},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":88,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":8,"checkedAt":1789021582031},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is a coherent Google Workspace integration, but it gives a third-party MCP server broad read/write account access through an unpinned auto-executed npm package and does not scope or warn about that access clearly enough.","dimensions":[{"detail":"For the stated purpose, access to Google Workspace is expected, but the combination of local package execution, stored OAuth credentials, and broad cloud-account read/write operations is high impact and under-scoped in the artifact.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Setup installs and configures an unpinned third-party npm package, then registers the server as `npx -y @presto-ai/google-workspace-mcp` with home scope, allowing future package resolution and execution outside the reviewed artifact.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The instructions disclose many available tools, but they frame setup as simple OAuth sign-in and do not clearly describe the requested OAuth scope breadth, account privacy impact, or confirmation expectations for write/delete/send actions.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill creates a persistent home-scoped MCP configuration and stores Google OAuth credentials under `~/.config/google-workspace-mcp/`; this is disclosed and removable, but it persists privileged account access beyond a single command.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The declared purpose matches the documented capabilities: Gmail, Calendar, Drive, Docs, Sheets, Slides, Chat, People, and auth tools are all Google Workspace functions. The capability set is broad and includes sending mail, modifying Gmail state, creating and editing documents, sending chat messages, and deleting calendar events.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Review this before installing if the Google account contains sensitive email, files, calendars, chats, or contacts. Prefer a dedicated or limited Google account, verify the npm package and publisher, pin a reviewed package version instead of using dynamic `npx -y`, and revoke/delete the stored OAuth credentials when no longer needed.","findings":"[PE3] expected: The `client_secret.json` references describe what this skill avoids in traditional Google API setup, and the credential storage path is disclosed OAuth behavior rather than artifact-backed credential theft.\n[TM1] expected: The `rm -rf ~/.config/google-workspace-mcp` command is a user-directed troubleshooting step scoped to deleting this integration's stored credentials, not an unbounded home-directory deletion.\n[SQP-2] unexpected: The concern is supported: the artifact lists broad read/write Workspace tools but lacks clear user-facing warnings about OAuth scope breadth and high-impact actions such as sending, modifying, and deleting account data.\n[RA2] expected: The cited draft-email example is not session persistence or a background agent mechanism; persistence is limited to the disclosed MCP config and OAuth credential storage.\n[EA1] expected: The phrase `run any command` means run another Google Workspace MCP command to trigger re-authentication, not arbitrary shell access; however, the overall tool catalog remains broad.\n[T08] unexpected: The static finding is supported by the install instructions: the package is unpinned and configured through `npx -y`, so the effective server code can change after review.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789021582031}}}}}